priority: 3
tags: event
max-visits: 1

= <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> joins the <span style="color: #BFC8CC;">**GNU**</span>

Walther Lambach and the <span style="color: #6D5298;">Christian Socials</span> have long championed a presidential government and the vision of a non-partisan strongman ruling above political factions. That strongman is Staal. With the formation of the <span style="color: #BFC8CC;">**GNU**</span>, he sees little remaining reason to maintain the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> as a political force.

He has urged his movement to merge into the <span style="color: #BFC8CC;">Commonwealth National Unity Front</span>, pointing to their shared goal of a <i>Volksgemeinschaft</i> that includes the workers and their common desire to cast off the chains of Etaluxia. Lambach and Trevannon, over the objections of old guard figures like Westmore and Hargen, have pushed the party at an emergency congress to vote for immediate dissolution—a vote that passes once a "monetary incentive" is offered to on the fence lower-level members by Staal himself.

- @schleicher_2: The <span style="color: #BFC8CC;">Commonwealth National Unity Front</span> welcomes its new member.

@schleicher_2
on-arrival: {!
Q.traditionalist_gnu = 1

Q.pro_republic -= Q.traditionalist_votes;

Q.traditionalist_relation = (Q.gnu_relation - 35);

Q.gnu_relation -= 15;

Q.gnu_r += Q.traditionalist_r;
Q.traditionalist_r = 0;
!}


